# Planes

Warm path: key → Chip 1 (`vt-engine`) → framed SOCK_STREAM → kernel PTY → bytes back → POD damage paint.

Forbidden on that path: JSON, cell dumps, per-cell String snapshots, SwiftUI Observation of the PTY buffer, SOCK_SEQPACKET, SCM_RIGHTS of the master, GUI posix_spawn of the user shell, drop-on-full PTY reads.

Kernel owns the PTY master and the byte history. Display dies on quit. Attach may classify; it must not paint. Orchestration JSON is cold.

Chip 0 / libghostty-vt is retired ([ADR 0054](../../docs/adr/0054-chip0-retired.md)). Domain sources must not name Ghostty FFI types.
